### When should you use Fractional Knapsack?

Use Fractional Knapsack when items are divisible and partial allocation is meaningful. In banking, this applies to capital allocation across partially fundable investments, distributing a fixed marketing budget across campaigns that accept any funding level, and splitting available liquidity across loan disbursements.

Do not use it when items are indivisible. Hiring decisions (you cannot hire half a person), server provisioning (you cannot provision half a machine), and selecting whole loan applications for approval are all 0/1 knapsack problems that require dynamic programming.

### What should a senior engineer know?

A senior engineer should be able to prove the greedy is optimal using an exchange argument. The proof states: if any optimal solution does not follow the density order, swapping capacity from a less dense item to a more dense one strictly improves the total value without exceeding capacity, contradicting the assumption that the original was optimal.

Senior engineers should also know that the fractional knapsack is a special case of linear programming. The LP relaxation of the integer 0/1 knapsack is exactly the fractional knapsack, which is why LP solvers use it as a bound in branch-and-bound algorithms for the integer version.

```java
// Exchange argument in pseudocode
// Suppose optimal O uses fraction f_A < 1 of item A (denser)
// and fraction f_B > 0 of item B (sparser)
// Transfer delta capacity from B to A:
//   new value = old value - delta*(vB/wB) + delta*(vA/wA)
//   Since vA/wA > vB/wB, the new value > old value
//   Contradiction: O was not optimal
```

### What are common interview follow-up questions?

Interviewers often ask these follow-ups after the fractional knapsack:

- What if items are indivisible? Then use 0/1 knapsack with DP.
- What if you can take unlimited copies? Then use unbounded knapsack DP.
- Can you solve it without sorting? A partial sort or quickselect on the pivot density can work if the knapsack fills with very few items.
- What is the relationship to linear programming? The fractional knapsack is the LP relaxation of the 0/1 integer program.
